    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f08d07b7_3207f62a",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/ISupplicant.hal",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-23T00:02:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@callflow(next\u003d{\"removeInterface\"}) on top of |createInterface| method? \n\nThis necessarily isn\u0027t the order. The client can chose to call any of the other methods in the interface after |createInterface|. I guess the only guaranteed callflow is that |removeInterface| should always be preceeded by a call to |createInterface|. But, i don\u0027t see a VTS annotation to state that.",
      "parentUuid": "f08d07b7_6cda83de",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 80,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 80,
        "endChar": 17
      },
